  "worked_solution": "We are given the signup rate $r(t)$ in users per day. To find the number of users that signed up between the times $t=3$ and $t=9$ days, we integrate $r(t)$ between these two limits. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{9}12\\cdot {2}^{t/3}\\,\\text{d}t & ={12\\cdot \\frac{3\\cdot {2}^{t/3}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}|}_{3}^{9} \\\\  & ={36\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{t/3}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}|}_{3}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}({2}^{3}-{2}^{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{216}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612} \\\\  & \u2248312\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer. \n\nTherefore, between $t=3$ and $t=9$ days, $312$ users signed up.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
